## URL Handling Standards

### CRITICAL: Always Normalize Base URLs

**Problem**: Double slashes (`//api/models`) break URLs and look unprofessional.

**Solution**: Always strip trailing slashes from base URLs before concatenating paths.

#### Frontend (TypeScript/JavaScript)
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Always normalize
const API_BASE = (import.meta.env.VITE_BACKEND_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3001').replace(/\/$/, '');
const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/models`);
```

```typescript
// ❌ WRONG - Don't use URL directly
const API_BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_BACKEND_API_URL || 'http://localhost:3001';
const response = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/models`);  // Creates double slash if env has trailing slash!
```

#### Backend (Python)
```python
# ✅ CORRECT - Strip trailing slashes
backend_url = os.getenv("BACKEND_API_URL", "https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com")
backend_url = backend_url.rstrip('/') if backend_url else "https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com"

# Then use it
f"{backend_url}/api/agents"
```

```python
# ❌ WRONG - Don't use URL directly
backend_url = os.getenv("BACKEND_API_URL", "https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com")
f"{backend_url}/api/agents"  # Creates double slash if env has trailing slash!
```

#### Shell Scripts
```bash
# ✅ CORRECT - No trailing slashes in URLs
BACKEND_URL="http://localhost:3001"

# ❌ WRONG - Don't add trailing slash
BACKEND_URL="http://localhost:3001/"
```

### Standard URL Formats

**Production**: `https://navi-j9a9.onrender.com` (no trailing slash)  
**Localhost**: `http://localhost:3001` (no trailing slash)  
**Consistency**: All base URLs follow the same pattern

## Common Mistakes to Avoid

1. ❌ **Using old JWT format for anon key**: Use `sb_publishable_` prefix
2. ❌ **Missing required headers**: Include `Authorization`, `apikey`, and `X-Supabase-Api-Version`
3. ❌ **Wrong phone format**: Use `+19729777432` not `"+19729777432"` in JSON
4. ❌ **Trying to use backend WebSocket**: It's been removed, use Supabase Realtime
5. ❌ **Forgetting RLS is enabled**: All frontend queries are filtered by user ID
6. ❌ **Using wrong database connection**: Use Session Pooler (port 5432) not Direct (IPv6 incompatible)
7. ❌ **Not normalizing base URLs**: Always strip trailing slashes to prevent double-slash bugs

## Testing

### Testing Workflow Changes (IMPORTANT!)

**CRITICAL**: Always check for and stop stale workers before testing workflow changes!

#### Step 1: Check for Running Workers

```bash
# Check if any workers are running
ps aux | grep "[p]ython worker.py"

# If any workers are found, STOP THEM:
pkill -9 -f "python worker.py"

# Verify they're stopped
ps aux | grep python | grep worker || echo "No workers running"
```

**Why this matters**: Old workers run stale code and will cause confusing bugs where your changes don't appear to work!

#### Step 2: Start Fresh Worker on Test Queue

```bash
cd agents
source venv/bin/activate
TASK_QUEUE="navi-agent-tasks-quicktest" python worker.py > /tmp/navi-worker.log 2>&1 &
```

**Important**: The test queue (`navi-agent-tasks-quicktest`) isolates your tests from production workers on Render!

#### Step 3: Use Quick Test Script

```bash
cd agents/scripts

# Create test agent (auto-starts worker on test queue)
./quick-test.sh          # Creates agent on test queue

# Test features
./quick-test.sh worker   # Manually restart worker on test queue
./quick-test.sh pause    # Pause agent
./quick-test.sh resume   # Resume agent  
./quick-test.sh status   # Check status (metrics, tokens, etc)
./quick-test.sh logs     # Watch worker logs (see emoji debug logs)

# Cleanup
./quick-test.sh delete   # Delete test agent and stop workflow
```

**Features**:
- ✅ Auto-starts worker on isolated test queue (navi-agent-tasks-quicktest)
- ✅ Kills any existing local workers before starting
- ✅ Caches auth token for 1 hour
- ✅ Remembers last test agent
- ✅ Quick pause/resume testing
- ✅ Live log tailing with debug output
- ✅ Automatic cleanup
- ✅ Safe from production workers on Render

#### Step 4: After Code Changes - RESTART THE WORKER!

```bash
# Stop old worker
pkill -9 -f "python worker.py"

# Start fresh worker with updated code
cd agents && source venv/bin/activate
TASK_QUEUE="navi-agent-tasks-quicktest" python worker.py > /tmp/navi-worker.log 2>&1 &

# Create new test agent (old ones have stale workflow code!)
cd scripts
./quick-test.sh delete   # Clean up old agent
./quick-test.sh          # Create fresh agent with new code
```

### Full End-to-End Test

```bash
cd agents/scripts
./e2e-test.sh  # Starts its own worker, runs full test, cleans up
```

**Use this for**: Complete validation before deployment (starts its own isolated worker)

### Backend Authentication Test
```bash
cd back-end
./test-auth.sh
```

### Manual Test with Token
```bash
cd back-end
./test-auth-manual.sh <ACCESS_TOKEN>
```

### Get Fresh Token
Use the curl commands at the top of this file with test credentials.

### Cleanup All Agents and Workers

**Clean up everything at once**:
```bash
cd back-end
npm run cleanup:all
```

**What it does**:
1. 🔪 Kills any local Python workers (on test queue or any queue)
2. 🔍 Finds all non-deleted agents in database
3. ⏹️  Terminates their Temporal workflows
4. 🗑️  Soft-deletes agents from database

**Environment variable**:
- `TEST_TASK_QUEUE`: Queue name to kill workers on (defaults to `navi-agent-tasks-quicktest`)

**Use this when**:
- Starting fresh after testing
- Cleaning up before deployment
- Workers are stuck or misbehaving
- You have orphaned agents in the database

### Common Testing Mistakes

1. ❌ **Forgetting to stop old workers** → Your changes won't run!
2. ❌ **Using production queue** → Production workers might steal your test workflows
3. ❌ **Not restarting worker after Python changes** → Stale code continues running
4. ❌ **Testing with old agents** → They're running old workflow code, create fresh ones!

## Key Files

- `back-end/src/server.ts` - Main Express server (REST API only)
